This repository is an overlay on the unmodified SGLang image lmsysorg/sglang:dev-dsv41. The overlay code, the
launcher, the watchdog, the decode bench, the row-partition tool and the documentation were written for this
repository; the third-party material below is included or adapted under its own licence.

Redistributed unmodified (vendor/, and baked into the published image at /opt/dsv41-spark/vendor):
  - b12x 1.3.0, the PyPI wheel, and a source snapshot of github.com/local-inference-lab/b12x at
    b58f34eaf978277621efced6678e6713fd7122e4. Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE in the archive). Both archives also hold
    two files under the BSD-3-Clause licence, kept with their notices: b12x/_lib/dense_gemm.py (NVIDIA CORPORATION &
    AFFILIATES) and b12x/attention/_shared/contiguous/forward.py (Jay Shah, Ganesh Bikshandi, Ying Zhang, Vijay
    Thakkar, Pradeep Ramani, Tri Dao). The snapshot is the byte-identical public archive; it keeps upstream's own
    development notes, which we do not use.
    Only b12x/comm/roce and b12x/comm/__init__.py are installed from the snapshot. Checksums in vendor/README.md.

Adapted third-party code (modified for this repository; the original notices apply to those parts):
  - overlay/roce_collectives.py: a port to SGLang's GroupCoordinator of the vLLM adapter b12x_roce_all_reduce.py by
    Jason (@original-el8), github.com/local-inference-lab/vllm pull request 597. Copyright contributors to the vLLM
    project. Apache License 2.0.
  - overlay/sm120_prefill_pages.py: the page re-split follows SGLang's _split_kv_pages_to_64 and calls SGLang's Triton
    kernels. overlay/served_aliases.py: the two route handlers mirror SGLang's http_server.py originals.
    Copyright SGLang Team. Apache License 2.0.
  - overlay/engram_staged.py: ported from the author's vLLM Engram-on-disk implementation, which builds on the
    tonyd2wild/Kai MIT disk path of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-vLLM-DGX-Spark (Copyright (c) 2026 Tech2wild, MIT License) and on
    vLLM's engram.py (Copyright contributors to the vLLM project, Apache License 2.0).
  - tools/engram_local.py and bench/needle.py: from github.com/tonyd2wild/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-vLLM-DGX-Spark
    (tools/engram_local.py, bench/v41needle.py) with small changes; bench/prefill_repetitive.py and bench/decode_bench.py
    reuse that file's request body and streaming loop. Copyright (c) 2026 Tech2wild. MIT License.

